  "design": {
    "reader": "apps/three-surface-poc/src/git-blob-batch.ts: readGitBlobsBatch spawns one 'git --no-optional-locks -C <root> cat-file --batch' with exactly the requested object names on stdin; parseGitCatFileBatch reads one answer per request in order. A missing, ambiguous or non-blob answer is that object's Error. Output ending before a header, an unexpected header, a body not followed by its newline (short or oversized), a full object id answered by another object, or output past the last request fails the whole batch. Names must be one non-empty line; an empty request spawns nothing.",
    "governanceSeam": "gitTreeReaders gains prefetch(paths): it batches only paths in the tree listing that are not yet cached, by '<commit>:<path>'. lifecycleFor calls it with exactly the names its loop reads (markdown, not the act's own record), before the loop. Successful bytes enter the existing cache; a per-object error is not cached, so the loop's read repeats it as the old single read and fails exactly as before. A batch that fails throws. Wired into loadBodyReadAuthorityInputs and loadWalkthroughJudgmentInputs; only when the tree reader is in use (an injected readFile disables it).",
    "injection": "LoadGovernanceInputsOptions.readGitBlobs is injectable. It defaults to the batch reader only when readGitBlob is also the default, so the existing hermetic tests (which inject single readers) never mix a fake single reader with real batched reads.",
    "selfCorpusSeam": "readSelfCorpus(repoRoot, revision, readBlobs = readGitBlobsBatch) requests the selected records' blob ids (non-blob entries are never requested and still throw self-corpus-nonblob), then each record takes its bytes from the batch; a missing or errored answer throws. The existing gitBlobObjectId integrity check is unchanged."
  },
  "readPopulation": {
    "successPath": "[Observed] Identical. The oracle test records every object the governance load reads with single reads only and with the batch, and requires the same set; the self-corpus oracle requires the requested ids to equal the selected sources' ids. Only Syzygy's own governance tree at the governance revision and the pinned self-corpus commit are read; no Butlers repository is touched.",
    "abortPath": "[Observed] in the code: When the lifecycle scan would abort part-way (a listed record that fails to decode as UTF-8), the batch has already fetched the remaining listed records of the same decisions directory at the same commit; the old loop stopped at the failing record. Likewise readSelfCorpus fetches all selected blobs before the first record that fails decoding or the object-id check. The fetched set never leaves the population the scan would read on success, nothing extra is returned, and the load still throws. This is disclosed rather than changed; no new path, repository or content class is read.",
    "authority": "No change to what the body-read gate evaluates: the oracle test requires loadBodyReadAuthorityInputs and evaluateBodyReadAuthority to be deep-equal with single and batched reads over the real tree."
  },
